\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)={{field-1}}+\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ {{field-2}}=-2{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)-{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-332814" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{{x}_{1}(t)+4{t}^{2}+2} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{-2{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)-4}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}+4L{{t}^{2}}+2L{1} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L{{x}_{1}(t)}+2L{{x}_{2}(t)}-4L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the results\n\n$$\nL{1}=\\frac{1}{s},\\,L{{t}^{2}}=\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}},\n$$\n\n we can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)={X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{8}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-3=-2{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)-\\frac{4}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-332814" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.d