problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{{field-1}}={{field-2}} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2=-{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s)-{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-332825" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{{x}_{1}(t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)-1}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}+2L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L{{x}_{1}(t)}+3L{{x}_{2}(t)}-L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the results\n\n$$\nL{1}=\\frac{1}{s},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9},\n$$\n\nwe can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)={X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}+9} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2=-{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s)-\\frac{1}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-332825" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture