stion" "q-332820" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "s{X}_{2}(s)-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-332820" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-332820" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{s}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-332820" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{s}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-332796" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+3{t}^{2}+1 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)-2,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{{field-1}}={{field-2}}+\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+1=-{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)-{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-332796" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{{x}_{1}(t)+3{t}^{2}+1} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)-2}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}+3L{{t}^{2}}+L{1} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L{{x}_{1}(t)}+4L{{x}_{2}(t)}-2L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the results\n\n$$\nL{1}=\\frac{1}{s},\\,L{{t}^{2}}=\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}},\n$$\n\n we can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1={X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{6}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+1=-{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)-\\frac{2}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-332796" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "52ebbb59ae57b409fe98e33775f7f70dc8d226e1c8dd6bea1d7bb615f02591de"} {"question" "q-332796" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-332796" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "s{X}_{1}(s)+1"] ["math" "s{X}_{1}(s)-1"] ["math" "{X}_{1}(s)+1"] ["math" "{X}_{1}(s)-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-332796" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "s{X}_{1}(s)-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-332796" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-332796" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{3}{{s}^{3}}"] ["math" "{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{4}{{s}^{3}}"] ["math" "{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}}"] ["math" "{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{6}{{s}^{3}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-332796" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{6}{{s}^{3}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-332796" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-332796" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{s}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-332796" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{s}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=5{x}_{2}(t)+2,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},$\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{s+2}{s(s-5)}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{5{x}_{2}(t)+2}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=2L{{x}_{1}(t)}+3L{{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=5L{{x}_{2}(t)}+2L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-0=2{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-1=5{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{2}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)},$ and we have used the fact that $L{1}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-1 & =5{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =1+\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{s+2}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{s+2}{s(s-5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s) & =2{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-2){X}_{1}(s) & =3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-2){X}_{1}(s) & =3(\\frac{s+2}{s(s-5)}) \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{3(s+2)}{s(s-5)(s-2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3(s+2)}{s(s-2)(s-5)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{s+2}{s(s-5)}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "52ebbb59ae57b409fe98e33775f7f70dc8d226e1c8dd6bea1d7bb615f02591de"} {"question" "q-333070" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333070" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3(s+2)}{s(s-2)(s-5)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{2}(t)+4,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}} $,\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2s+4}{s(s-3)}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{3{x}_{2}(t)+4}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}+2L{{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=3L{{x}_{2}(t)}+4L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1={X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2=3{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{4}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)},$ and we have used the fact that $L{1}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-2 & =3{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =2+\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+4}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+4}{s(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1 & ={X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =2{X}_{2}(s)-1 \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =2(\\frac{2s+4}{s(s-3)})-1 \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{4s+8}{s(s-3)}-1 \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{4s+8-s(s-3)}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{4s+8-{s}^{2}+3s}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+7s+8}{s(s-3)} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+7s+8}{s(s-1)(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{-{s}^{2}+7s+8}{s(s-1)(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2s+4}{s(s-3)}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "52ebbb59ae57b409fe98e33775f7f70dc8d226e1c8dd6bea1d7bb615f02591de"} {"question" "q-333064" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333064" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{-s^{2}+7s+8}{s(s-1)(s-3)}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-332784" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+5 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{s+5}{s(s+1)},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-332784" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{-{x}_{1}(t)+5} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{2{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=-L{{x}_{1}(t)}+5L{1} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=2L{{x}_{1}(t)}+4L{{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1=-{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+1=2{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)},$ and we have used the fact that $L{1}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1 & =-{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ (s+1){X}_{1}(s) & =1+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ (s+1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{s+5}{s} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{s+5}{s(s+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)+1 & =2{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =2{X}_{1}(s)-1 \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =2(\\frac{s+5}{s(s+1)})-1 \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2(s+5)-s(s+1)}{s(s+1)} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+s+10}{s(s+1)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+s+10}{s(s+1)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system  in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{s+5}{s(s+1)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-{s}^{2}+s+10}{s(s+1)(s-4)}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-332784" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "52ebbb59ae57b409fe98e33775f7f70dc8d226e1c8dd6bea1d7bb615f02591de"} {"question" "q-332784" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-332784" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{-s^{2}+s+10}{s(s+1)(s-4)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{2}(t)+6,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},$\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{6-s}{s(s-4)}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{-3{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{4{x}_{2}(t)+6}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=-3L{{x}_{1}(t)}+L{{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=4L{{x}_{2}(t)}+6L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2=-3{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+1=4{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{6}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)},$ and we have used the fact that $L{1}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)+1 & =4{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{6}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =-1+\\frac{6}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-s+6}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{6-s}{s(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2 & =-3{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s+3){X}_{1}(s) & =2+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s+3){X}_{1}(s) & =2+(\\frac{6-s}{s(s-4)}) \\\\ (s+3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2s(s-4)+6-s}{s(s-4)} \\\\ (s+3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2({s}^{2}-4s)+6-s}{s(s-4)} \\\\ (s+3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-8s+6-s}{s(s-4)} \\\\ (s+3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-9s+6}{s(s-4)} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-9s+6}{s(s-4)(s+3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}-9s+6}{s(s-4)(s+3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{6-s}{s(s-4)}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "52ebbb59ae57b409fe98e33775f7f70dc8d226e1c8dd6bea1d7bb615f02591de"} {"question" "q-333071" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333071" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2s^{2}-9s+6}{s(s-4)(s+3)}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333073" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{2}(t)+1,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},$\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2s+1}{s(s-3)}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333073" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{4{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{3{x}_{2}(t)+1}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=4L{{x}_{1}(t)}+L{{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=3L{{x}_{2}(t)}+L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1=4{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2=3{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{1}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)},$ and we have used the fact that $L{1}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-2 & =3{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =2+\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+1}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+1}{s(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1 & =4{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =1+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =1+(\\frac{2s+1}{s(s-3)}) \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{s(s-3)+2s+1}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-3s+2s+1}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-s+1}{s(s-3)} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-s+1}{s(s-3)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}-s+1}{s(s-3)(s-4)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2s+1}{s(s-3)}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333073" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "52ebbb59ae57b409fe98e33775f7f70dc8d226e1c8dd6bea1d7bb615f02591de"} {"question" "q-333073" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333073" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{s^{2}-s+1}{s(s-3)(s-4)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-330958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+3 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{3}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1/2}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{3/2}{s-3}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-330958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{3}{s}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}}-3{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t}-3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{t}-3 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1/2}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{3/2}{s-3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}+\\frac{3}{2}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{1\\cdot t}-1+\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{3\\cdot t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{t}+\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{3t}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t}-3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{t}+\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{3t}-1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-330958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "52ebbb59ae57b409fe98e33775f7f70dc8d226e1c8dd6bea1d7bb615f02591de"} {"question" "q-330958" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-330958" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e^{t}-3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-330958" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-330958" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}e^{t}-1+\\frac{3}{2}e^{3t}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333134" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)+2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{2}{s-1}+\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s-2}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333134" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{s-1}+\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s}} \\\\  & =2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}}-2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{1\\cdot t}+{e}^{2\\cdot t}-2 \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}+2{e}^{t}-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t}+2{e}^{t}-2 \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333134" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "52ebbb59ae57b409fe98e33775f7f70dc8d226e1c8dd6bea1d7bb615f02591de"} {"question" "q-333134" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333134" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2e^{t}+e^{2t}-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333134" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333134" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e^{2t}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333133" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+9{x}_{2}(t)+9 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{2}(t)+2,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{3}{s-2},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{1}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333133" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{3}{s-2}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}}+3\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{-1\\cdot t}+3{e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{-t}+3{e}^{2t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\cdot t}-1 \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{2t}+{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}-1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333133" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "52ebbb59ae57b409fe98e33775f7f70dc8d226e1c8dd6bea1d7bb615f02591de"} {"question" "q-333133" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333133" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e^{-t}+3e^{2t}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333133" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333133" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e^{2t}-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333137" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+9{x}_{2}(t)-20 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{2}(t)-2,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{2}{s+2}+\\frac{3}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s-1}+\\frac{2}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333137" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{s+2}+\\frac{3}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}}+3\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2\\cdot t}+3{e}^{1\\cdot t}-1 \\\\  & =3{e}^{t}-1+2{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}+\\frac{2}{s}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}}+2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t}+2 \\\\  & ={e}^{t}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{t}-1+2{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{t}+2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333137" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "52ebbb59ae57b409fe98e33775f7f70dc8d226e1c8dd6bea1d7bb615f02591de"} {"question" "q-333137" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333137" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2e^{-2t}+3e^{t}-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333137" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333137" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e^{t}+2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+6{x}_{2}(t)+2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{2}(t)-1,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=-\\frac{2}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{s-2}+\\frac{2}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s+1}-\\frac{1}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{-\\frac{2}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{s-2}+\\frac{2}{s}} \\\\  & =-2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}}+2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{-1\\cdot t}+{e}^{2\\cdot t}+2 \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}+2-2{e}^{-t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}-\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={e}^{-1\\cdot t}-1 \\\\  & =-1+{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t}+2-2{e}^{-t} \\\\ -1+{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "52ebbb59ae57b409fe98e33775f7f70dc8d226e1c8dd6bea1d7bb615f02591de"} {"question" "q-333138" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333138" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2e^{-t}+e^{2t}+2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333138" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "q-333138" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e^{-t}-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/state.json" "file_sha256" "394c25f88232ee568e0ce2171afd038799b3c5ebb8694f75c8b7afe92251dadb"} {"question" "e-21575" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/assets/8161123eafa5ed80dc37b8e017c5598fcacaf241a84a09ca27f73d204d7b0e74.png)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, find the system of equations." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/example-21575.json" "file_sha256" "35b976c19f95250a727c98c49c519b6cc39832b0c4d3f932e29aefe1cf2d0ac7"} {"question" "e-21575" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{2{x}_{1}(t)+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-3} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{-3{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=2L{{x}_{1}(t)}+5L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)}-3L{1} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=-3L{{x}_{1}(t)}+4L{{x}_{2}(t)}+2L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the results\n\n$$\n\\mathcal L\\{1\\} = \\dfrac{1}{s}, \\quad\n\\mathcal L\\{\\cos(2t)\\} = \\dfrac{s}{s^2+4}, \\quad\n\\mathcal L\\{\\sin(2t)\\} = \\dfrac{2}{s^2+4},\n$$\n\nwe can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1=2{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{5s}{{s}^{2}+4}-\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+2=-3{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t),$ respectively." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/example-21575.json" "file_sha256" "35b976c19f95250a727c98c49c519b6cc39832b0c4d3f932e29aefe1cf2d0ac7"} {"question" "e-21576" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/assets/ce973be1a5a98fa04fad06c1ca5ee19c7f1b0cfd421d0cd449c7cb52138bf9bd.png)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$  find the solution of the new system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/example-21576.json" "file_sha256" "c492c9c73cbcd5272af9c1b87b25234c4bef21e2de17331c9d1a484f058608ff"} {"question" "e-21576" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{-{x}_{1}(t)+4} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{2{x}_{1}(t)-3{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=-L{{x}_{1}(t)}+4L{1} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=2L{{x}_{1}(t)}-3L{{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1=-{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-0=2{X}_{1}(s)-3{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\},$ and we have used the fact that $\\mathcal L\\{1\\} = \\dfrac1s.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for $X_1(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1 & =-{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ (s+1){X}_{1}(s) & =1+\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ (s+1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{s+4}{s} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{s+4}{s(s+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for $X_2(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s) & =2{X}_{1}(s)-3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s+3){X}_{2}(s) & =2{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ (s+3){X}_{2}(s) & =2(\\frac{s+4}{s(s+1)}) \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2(s+4)}{s(s+1)(s+3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\nX_1(s) = \\dfrac{s+4}{s(s+1)} ,\\qquad \nX_2(s) = \\dfrac{2(s+4)}{s(s+1)(s+3)}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/example-21576.json" "file_sha256" "c492c9c73cbcd5272af9c1b87b25234c4bef21e2de17331c9d1a484f058608ff"} {"question" "e-21577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/assets/a699a4e262534557453aaa9e44d1b273dd4489190e50cec8f9ef9e0da91e7d29.png)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\nX_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\} = -\\dfrac{1}{s+2} + \\dfrac{2}{s-1} - \\dfrac{2}{s}, \\qquad\nX_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\} = \\dfrac{1}{s+2} + \\dfrac{3}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/example-21577.json" "file_sha256" "1a1fb14af645fcebae622f66035f744ec05b67bafbe427b1a4168ab19952a4b3"} {"question" "e-21577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to $X_1(s)$ and $X_2(s){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{-\\frac{1}{s+2}+\\frac{2}{s-1}-\\frac{2}{s}} \\\\  & =-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}}+2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}}-2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2\\cdot t}+2{e}^{1\\cdot t}-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2{e}^{t}-{e}^{-2t}-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}+\\frac{3}{s}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}}+3\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2\\cdot t}+3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{-2t}+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{t}-{e}^{-2t}-2 \\\\ {e}^{-2t}+3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/example-21577.json" "file_sha256" "1a1fb14af645fcebae622f66035f744ec05b67bafbe427b1a4168ab19952a4b3"}] "usage" {"e-21577" [] "e-21576" [] "q-333064" [] "e-21575" [] "q-330958" []} "basis" 2773 "retractions" [[17592186167170 :question/problem "${x_{1}^{′}(t) = x_{1}(t) + 2x_{2}(t); x_{2}^{′}(t) = 3x_{2}(t) + 4,x(0) = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables $X_{1}(s) = L{x_{1}(t)}$ and $X_{2}(s) = L{x_{2}(t)}$. In terms of the parameter $s$, the solution of the new system is$X_{1}(s) =$ {{field-1}} $$,\n$X_{2}(s) = (2s + 4)/(s(s - 3))$.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"solving-an-initial-value-problem-given-the-laplace-transformed-solution\"></a>"] [17592186167127 :question/problem "${x_{1}^{′}(t) = x_{1}(t) + 3; x_{2}^{′}(t) =-x_{1}(t) + 3x_{2}(t),x(0) = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution\n$X_{1}(s) = L{x_{1}(t)} = \\frac{1}{s - 1} - \\frac{3}{s}, X_{2}(s) = L{x_{2}(t)} = \\frac{1/2}{s - 1} - \\frac{1}{s} + \\frac{3/2}{s - 3}$.\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t) =$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |"] [17592186166462 :question/problem "${x_{1}^{′}(t) = 2x_{1}(t) + 5\\cos (2t) - 3; x_{2}^{′}(t) =-3x_{1}(t) + 4x_{2}(t) + 2\\sin (2t)$,\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, find the system of equations."] [17592186166462 :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{L{x_{1}^{′}(t)} = L{2x_{1}(t) + 5\\cos (2t) - 3}; L{x_{2}^{′}(t)} = L{-3x_{1}(t) + 4x_{2}(t) + 2\\sin (2t)}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{sL{x_{1}(t)} - x_{1}(0) = 2L{x_{1}(t)} + 5L{\\cos (2t)} - 3L{1}; sL{x_{2}(t)} - x_{2}(0) =-3L{x_{1}(t)} + 4L{x_{2}(t)} + 2L{\\sin (2t)}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the results\n\n$$\n\\mathcal L\\{1\\} = \\dfrac{1}{s}, \\quad \\mathcal L\\{\\cos(2t)\\} = \\dfrac{s}{s^2+4}, \\quad \\mathcal L\\{\\sin(2t)\\} = \\dfrac{2}{s^2+4}\n$$\n\nwe can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n{sX_{1}(s) - 1 = 2X_{1}(s) + \\frac{5s}{s^{2} + 4} - \\frac{3}{s}; sX_{2}(s) + 2 =-3X_{1}(s) + 4X_{2}(s) + \\frac{4}{s^{2} + 4}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nX_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{x_1(t) \\right\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nX_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{x_2(t) \\right\\}\n$$\n\nare the Laplace transforms of the functions $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t)$, respectively."] [17592186166463 :question/problem "${x_{1}^{′}(t) =-x_{1}(t) + 4; x_{2}^{′}(t) = 2x_{1}(t) - 3x_{2}(t)$,\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{x_2(t) \\right\\}$. In terms of the parameter $s$, find the solution of the new system."] [17592186166463 :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{L{x_{1}^{′}(t)} = L{-x_{1}(t) + 4}; L{x_{2}^{′}(t)} = L{2x_{1}(t) - 3x_{2}(t)}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{sL{x_{1}(t)} - x_{1}(0) =-L{x_{1}(t)} + 4L{1}; sL{x_{2}(t)} - x_{2}(0) = 2L{x_{1}(t)} - 3L{x_{2}(t)}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{sX_{1}(s) - 1 =-X_{1}(s) + \\frac{4}{s}; sX_{2}(s) - 0 = 2X_{1}(s) - 3X_{2}(s)\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nX_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{x_1(t) \\right\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nX_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{x_2(t) \\right\\}\n$$\n\nand we have used the fact that\n\n$$\n\\mathcal L\\{1\\} = \\dfrac1s\n$$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for $X_1(s)$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nsX_{1}(s) - 1 &= -X_{1}(s) + \\frac{4}{s} \\\\\n(s + 1)X_{1}(s) &= 1 + \\frac{4}{s} \\\\\n(s + 1)X_{1}(s) &= \\frac{s + 4}{s} \\\\\nX_{1}(s) &= (s + 4)/(s(s + 1))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for $X_2(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nsX_{2}(s) &= 2X_{1}(s) - 3X_{2}(s) \\\\\n(s + 3)X_{2}(s) &= 2X_{1}(s) \\\\\n(s + 3)X_{2}(s) &= 2((s + 4)/(s(s + 1))) \\\\\nX_{2}(s) &= (2(s + 4))/(s(s + 1)(s + 3))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is\n\n$$\nX_1(s) = \\dfrac{s+4}{s(s+1)},\\qquad X_2(s) = \\dfrac{2(s+4)}{s(s+1)(s+3)}\n$$"] [17592186166464 :question/problem "${x_{1}^{′}(t) = x_{1}(t) + 3x_{2}(t) - 7; x_{2}^{′}(t) =-2x_{2}(t) + 6$,\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution\n$X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{x_1(t) \\right\\} = -\\dfrac{1}{s+2} + \\dfrac{2}{s-1} - \\dfrac{2}{s}, \\qquad X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{x_2(t) \\right\\} = \\dfrac{1}{s+2} + \\dfrac{3}{s}$.\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem."] [17592186166464 :question/worked-solution "To find $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to $X_1(s)$ and $X_2(s){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1}(t) &= L^{-1}{X_{1}(s)} \\\\\n&= L^{-1}{-\\frac{1}{s + 2} + \\frac{2}{s - 1} - \\frac{2}{s}} \\\\\n&=-L^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s + 2}} + 2L^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s - 1}} - 2L^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\\n&=-e^{-2 \\cdot t} + 2e^{1 \\cdot t} - 2 \\cdot 1 \\\\\n&= 2e^{t} - e^{-2t} - 2 \\\\\nx_{2}(t) &= L^{-1}{X_{2}(s)} \\\\\n&= L^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s + 2} + \\frac{3}{s}} \\\\\n&= L^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s + 2}} + 3L^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\\n&= e^{-2 \\cdot t} + 3 \\cdot 1 \\\\\n&= e^{-2t} + 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx(t) &= \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1}(t) \\\\ x_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}2e^{t} - e^{-2t} - 2 \\\\ e^{-2t} + 3\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [[17592186164123 :answer-field/id] [17592186164123 :answer-field/key] [17592186164123 :answer-field/type] [17592186164124 :answer-field/id] [17592186164124 :answer-field/key] [17592186164124 :answer-field/type] [17592186164431 :answer-field/id] [17592186164431 :answer-field/key] [17592186164431 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
